# GT6 recipes: no stand-in ingredients

Java/tick source of truth remains local `gt6_code/gregtech6`. Do not fetch
GitHub. Search that tree (it is gitignored; see `gt6-local-source-search`).
Translate names with `python tools/gt6_resolve.py` before treating a part as
missing.

A shaped/shapeless/machine recipe is complete only when every grid/slot is
the same GT6 object after registry-name translation (`OP.wireGt01` → CC
`wire`, `MT.Os` → `osmium_elemental`). `ANY.Cu` may land on a copper-family
member, never an unrelated metal.

**Forbidden** (this is how battery cells were faked with plates/dust/rods):

- Replace a missing part with a different material, prefix, vanilla item, or
  a single `programmed_circuit` so the machine is "survival craftable".
- Invent geometry, collapse `OD_CIRCUITS[tier]`, or write
  「缺形态时 DESIGN_POLICY 用已有材料做生存获得」 in a new/active plan.
- Treat creative-tab access or "players can still assemble something" as
  `player_complete`.

If any ingredient is missing: do not emit a stand-in recipe; keep
`runtime_ready`; record the missing part as `blocked` / gap. Either add the
real part in-scope or leave the recipe unimplemented.

Closed-card stand-ins are not stable. When the real GT6 part exists, replace
the fake grid/slot on the next touching change — do not wait for a reclaim
card. Do not invent a new stand-in to keep a closed `player_complete` green.

Art placeholders are a separate rule (`gt6-art-no-placeholder`).
Catalog `ItemEntity` worldgen as obtain is a separate rule
(`gt6-no-item-entity-worldgen-acquisition`).
